Free the decompressed buffer when closing an LZMA read stream

closeb_lzma frees p->bf only in write mode. In read mode, bf holds the
whole decompressed input, allocated by add_lzma_decompressor, so every
read-side close leaks it. The runtime closes the combinator stream right
after parsing it, and each .mhscache read goes through the same path, so
a process that loads code repeatedly leaks one buffer per load (10-20MB
for a program that pulls in base).

--- a/src/runtime/bfile.c
+++ b/src/runtime/bfile.c
@@ -1895,8 +1895,9 @@
   if (!p->read) {
     /* Write mode: compress whatever is buffered. */
     flushb_lzma(bp);
-    bfbuffer_free(&p->bf);
   }
+  /* Both modes own bf: read mode holds the decompressed input */
+  bfbuffer_free(&p->bf);
   closeb(p->bfile);
   FREE(p);
 }
